{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-27T11:04:09.176Z","author":"pm-github","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"49285cdb3ae2c9d3a7c09636","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/body","value":"## Problem\n\nSince 2026-11-23, CodeQL has reported three open `js/polynomial-redos` alerts on `main`:\n\n- **#2** `src/selectors.ts:28`: the ATX heading regex `^(#{1,6})[ \\t]+(.+?)[ \\t]*#*[ \\t]*\\r?$` in `paragraph()`.\n- **#3** `src/selectors.ts:55`: the same regex in `sectionPath()`.\n- **#1** `src/json-spans.ts:13`: the sticky token matcher used by `parseSpans()`.\n\nThe heading pattern has a lazy `.+?` followed by three optional runs (`[ \\t]*#*[ \\t]*`). On a long heading line made of spaces and `#`, it backtracks polynomially. Cited documents are agent-supplied input, so a hostile or merely large transcript can stall evidence verification.\n\n## Expected\n\n- Parse ATX headings in one linear pass per line, without a backtracking regex. Keep today's semantics exactly:\n  - 1–6 `#` followed by at least one space or tab;\n  - an optional closing `#` sequence, stripped only when preceded by a space or tab (CommonMark);\n  - trailing whitespace and `\\r` stripped;\n  - a heading made of only a closing sequence yields an empty title.\n- `paragraph()` and `sectionPath()` share that one parser.\n- Make the JSON span tokenizer provably linear, or show with a test that CodeQL's flagged path is linear and dismiss the alert with that justification in the PR, not silently.\n- All three alerts close on the PR's CodeQL run.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- Table-driven tests compare the new heading parser with the old regex on a corpus of normal, edge and CommonMark example headings (identical results), and the tests fail on revert.\n- An adversarial-input test, for example 50,000 spaces and `#` on one line and a 1 MB JSON string with escapes, finishes within a small fixed time budget on the new code. Under the old regex, the same test demonstrably exceeds that budget.\n- The existing test suite and coverage thresholds are unchanged."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-evidence-github-cc12c36f952a-86"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Three CodeQL polynomial-ReDoS alerts: ATX heading regex in selectors and the JSON span tokenizer"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"GH issue #86: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-evidence/issues/86 · author @unbraind · created 2026-11-27T10:54:17Z · updated 2026-11-27T10:54:17Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["gh:unbraind/pm-evidence#86","github_author:unbraind"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-27T11:04:09.176Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-27T11:04:09.176Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"pm-github"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"72256f103377503ccc27d002b04443fd14a8e952bc7f72d6a6ccb62f150d0f60","item_hash_version":3,"message":"Imported from GitHub #86","event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"e6ee8ad335e9c5d9d0118b1ad05fad43be7bba60a494ad34b92e1a6de8185c1b"}
