{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-27T11:05:09.295Z","author":"codex-agent","author_source":"configured","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"49285cdb3ae2c9d3a7c09636","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-27T11:05:09.295Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-11-27T11:05:09.295Z","author":"codex-agent","text":"Claimed. Plan: (1) reproduce the three polynomial-ReDoS paths with a timing harness, (2) replace the backtracking ATX heading regex with a single-pass linear parser shared by paragraph() and sectionPath(), (3) make the JSON span tokenizer provably linear (regex-free scanning), (4) table-driven equivalence tests against the old regex plus adversarial timing tests that fail on revert, (5) rebuild dist, run targeted gates, PR."}]}],"before_hash":"c45fe3b18841964db50d945bdda86fde87e08ead0426326798a55deb0bde44c7","after_hash":"a587c7b2a713596a4de77c8b9777d35284a66d41ad633ea6e772aa7cc6bf492f","item_hash_version":3,"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"3bfbd2dae13bb186c7099db011d1639725144ddf0329b035b271850673a9cd9b"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-27T11:30:39.166Z","author":"codex-agent","author_source":"configured","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"49285cdb3ae2c9d3a7c09636","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-27T11:30:39.164Z","author":"codex-agent","text":"Reproduction confirmed on the retired heading regex: 800-char hostile space run => 1.7s, 1600 => 13.1s (~n^2.8 growth); a 50,000-char line extrapolates to hours, so cited-document verification stalls. The retired JSON tokenizer measured LINEAR on every adversarial probe (1MB escaped string 0.03ms, 500k escape pairs 0.2ms, 1MB digits 0.1ms, 1MB whitespace 220ms via a per-char regex test) - alert #1 is analyzed as a CodeQL false positive on an unambiguous alternation, but the tokenizer is rewritten regex-free anyway so the alert closes mechanically and linearity is provable by construction. Design: (1) new single-pass per-line ATX parser (headingLines) shared by paragraph() and sectionPath(), byte-identical to the retired regex (proven by curated corpus + 400 seeded random documents); it reproduces the exact lazy-title and CR-swallow span semantics; (2) json-spans.ts scanner has no regex at all: code-unit string/number/literal scanning, JSON.parse still decodes object keys; (3) new tests: heading-parity.test.ts (corpus + differential + 50k budget + retired-regex child probe killed at 400ms), json-spans-linear.test.ts (string-token differential vs the retired sticky regex + hostile budgets incl. the 8MB whitespace that fails on revert); (4) two function-scope revert cases added to the repo's revert harness, both yielding negativeControl fail 1."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-27T11:30:39.166Z"}],"before_hash":"a587c7b2a713596a4de77c8b9777d35284a66d41ad633ea6e772aa7cc6bf492f","after_hash":"809a46b1dc4dddce7362b1ee7b895ec385d4e221f9ab3a446800a84883fc7f34","item_hash_version":3,"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"882e0b777e6402eb0318ee80f78ceb61ccb1f474f52e8bc3e158b9c83dd51b32"}
